<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maun is a town in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, on the Thamalakane river at the south-eastern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okavango-delta">Okavango Delta</a>. It became the capital of the Batawana in 1915 and is the administrative centre of the North-West District. It is the main base for tourism in the delta.</p></div>
